      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is given by $⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ Find $⟨x,y⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-3-3+2 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
